 surpasses a threshold set to be excessively high in the system parameters.","27":"Spare","28":"Alarm is triggered if the turbine is not closed, while the Unit is in the state that dictates that the turbine should be closed.","29":"Alarm is triggered when the measurement surpasses the high-value threshold set in the system parameters, or digital signal is indicating that the measured value has high value.","30":"Alarm is triggered if the wicket gate disturbance sensor declares that one or more wicket gates have disturbed position.","31":"Alarm is triggered when the measurement surpasses a threshold set to be excessively high in the system parameters, or digital signal is indicating that the measured value has very high value.","32":"Alarm is triggered when the contactor activation command is activated, and the contactor does not carry out the requested operation within the time limit set in system parameters. Conversely, an alarm is also triggered when the contactor activation command is not activated, and the contactor is on. This could be due to intentional handling, wire break or a malfunction of the contactor or auxiliary contacts.","33":"Alarm is triggered when circuit breaker is off. This could be due to intentional handling, wire break or a malfunction of auxiliary contacts.","34":"Alarm is triggered when circuit breaker is tripped. This could be due to protection activation, wire break or a malfunction of auxiliary contacts.","35":"Spare","36":"Spare","37":"Spare","38":"Alarm is triggered when the contactor activation command is activated, and the contactor does not carry out the requested operation within the time limit set in system parameters. Conversely, an alarm is also triggered when the contactor activation command is not activated, and the contactor is on. This could be due to intentional handling, wire break or a malfunction of the contactor or auxiliary contacts.","39":"Alarm is triggered when circuit breaker is off. This could be due to intentiona