on of second valve in speed up.","524":"Value that declares speed in which \u0022speed up\u0022 transitions to the next point.","525":"Position of first valve in speed up.","526":"Position of second valve in speed up.","527":"Value that declares speed in which \u0022speed up\u0022 transitions to the next point.","528":"0 - Synchronizer giving up/down signals, 1 - Speed reference following grid frequency","529":"Value that declares the increment of speed reference due to synchronizer command.","530":"Value that declares the reference of the deflector valve at minimum power before switching on the regulation.","531":"Value that declares the reference of the synchronization nozzle at minimum power before switching on the regulation.","532":"1 - Water level, 3 - Active power, 4 - Position ","533":"Value that declares ramp time of first valve in case of normal shutdown.","534":"Value that declares ramp time of first valve in case of quick shutdown.","535":"Value that declares ramp time of first valve in case of emergency shutdown.","536":"Value that declares ramp time of second valve in case of normal shutdown.","537":"Value that declares ramp time of second valve in case of quick shutdown.","538":"Value that declares ramp time of second valve in case of emergency shutdown.","539":"","540":"","541":"A value that declares the speed below which a turbine fault is considered if this speed is not reached within the given time.","542":"Value that declares minimal openness of valves while power plant is connected to the grid.","543":"Value that declares minimal water level below which shutdown is activated. Power plant restarts automatically when water level rises above given limit.","544":"","545":"","546":"","547":"","548":"","549":"Parameter used to declare lowest value of analog control signal range.","550":"Parameter used to declare highest value of analog control signal range.","551":"Constant value added to or subtracted from control signal to shift it to the desired reference point.","552":"Constant multiplier used to scale or transform the magnitude of the control signal to achieve the desired system response.","553":"","554":"","555":"","556":"","557":"","558":"Ramping time which uses algoritam fo nozzle selection to keep constant flow during nozzle switching.","559":"Hysteresis of turbine flow on which algoritam of nozzle selection is deactivated.","560":"Maximal turbine flow","561":"Value that declares a position of nozzle 1 at which nozzle 2 is deactivated.","562":"Value that declares a position of nozzle 1 at which nozzle 2 is activated.","563":"Value that is added to \u0022Nozzle 2 deactivation point\u0022 to guard system from unexpected activations/deactivations of certain nozzles.","564":"Value that declares a position of nozzle 2 at which nozzle 3 is deactivated.","565":"Value that declares a position of nozzle 2 at which nozzle 3 is activated.","566":"Value that is added to \u0022Nozzle 3 deactivation point\u0022 to guard system from unexpected activations/deactivations of certain nozzles.","567":"Value that declares a position of nozzle 3 at which nozzle 4 is deactivated.","568":"Value that declares a position of nozzle 3 at which nozzle 4 is activated.","569":"Value that is added to \u0022Nozzle 4 deactivation point\u0022 to guard system from unexpected activations/deactivations of certain nozzles.","570":"Value that declares a position of nozzle 4 at which nozzle 5 is deactivated.","571":"Value that declares a position of nozzle 4 at which nozzle 5 is activated.","572":"Value that is added to \u0022Nozzle 5 deactivation point\u0022 to guard system from unexpected activations/deactivations of certain nozzles.","573":"Value that declares a position of nozzle 5 at which nozzle 6 is deactivated.","574":"Value that declares a position of nozzle 5 at which nozzle 6 is activated.","575":"Value that is added to \u0022Nozzle 6 deactivation point\u0022 to guard system from unexpected activations/deactivations of certain nozzles.","576":"","577":"","578":"","579":"","580":"","581":"","582":"","583":"","584":"","585":"","586":"","587":"","588":"","589":"","590":"","591":"","592":"","593":"","594":"","595":"","596":"","597":"","598":"","599":"","600":"","601":"","602":"","603":"","604":"","605":"","606":"","607":"","608":"Low limit of output value.","609":"High limit of output value.","610":"Limit for slew rate of the output value in second in positive range with falling absolute value.","611":"Limit for slew rate of the output value in second in positive range with rising absolute value.","612":"Limit for slew rate of the output value in second in positive range with falling absolute value.","613":"Limit for slew rate of the output value in second in positive range with rising absolute value.","614":"If the input \u0022Enable manual mode\u0022 is set then the control loop is interrupted. A manual value \u2028is set as the manipulated value.","615":"The PID actions can be switched on and off individually in the PID algorithm. P-action is on when the \u0022Enable P-action\u0022 input is set.","616":"The PID actions can be switched on and off individually in the PID algorithm. I action is on when the input \u0022I-action on\u0022 is set.","617":"The output of the integral action can be frozen. For this the input \u0022I-action hold\u0022 must be set.","618":"The PID actions can be switched on and off individually in the PID algorithm. D-action is on when the ?input \u0022Enable D-action\u0022 is set.","619":"The \u0022number of cycles\u0022 in PID parameters refers to number of times the PID function is called in PLC. The time duration of one function is predetermined so that it is possible to calculate the total duration of the call.","620":"The \u0022Proportional gain\u0022 input specifies controller amplification.","621":"The \u0022Integration time\u0022 input determines the time ?response of the integral action.","622":"The \u0022Derivative action time\u0022 input determines the time response of the derivative action.","623":"Time lag of the D-action, the algorithm of the D-action contains a delay for which parameters can be assigned at the input \u0022Time lag of the D-action\u0022.","624":"A dead band is applied to the system deviation. The \u0022Dead band width\u0022 input determines the size of the dead band.","625":"The manipulated value is always restricted to a high limit and low limit. The \u0022High limit of manipulated value\u0022 input specifies the high limit.","626":"The manipulated value is always restricted to a high limit and low limit. The \u0022Low limit of manipulated value\u0022 input specifies the low limit.","627":"The \u0022Process value factor\u0022 input is multiplied by the process value. The input is used to scale the process value range.","628":"The input \u0022Process value offset\u0022 is added to the process value. The input is used to scale the process value range.","629":"The \u0022Manipulated value factor\u0022 input is multiplied with the manipulated value. The input is used to scale the manipulated value range.","630":"The input \u0022Manipulated value offset\u0022 is added to the process value. The input is used to scale the manipulated value range.","631":"For feedforward control, the disturbance variable is interconnected to the \u0022Disturbance variable\u0022 input.","632":"The \u0022Manual value\u0022 input is used to set a ?manual value using the operator interface ?functions.","633":"The \u0022Reference correction\u0022 value dynamically modifies the desired setpoint or target value based on external conditions or feedback, allowing the PID controller to adapt and maintain precise control in varying situations.","634":"Value that declares if PID output is analog or digital signal.","635":"","636":"","637":"","638":"","639":"","640":"Low limit of output value.","641":"High limit of output value.","642":"Limit for slew rate of the output value in second in positive range with falling absolute value.","643":